From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu Yuwei <yuweiwu@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:43:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Lay out tabs at tab stops

`StyleProperty::TabStops` (`TextStyle::tab_stops`): the distance between tab
stops and the least a tab advances, which the embedder works out (CSS
`tab-size`). `None` by default: a tab keeps the advance it was shaped with,
as before.

The line breaker gives a tab the advance to the next tab stop from where it
is on its line; the min/max-content measurer works it out on each of its two
lines. The shaper also shapes a tab as a space, so that it draws nothing:
few fonts map U+0009.
